@@ -8,6 +8,19 @@ package, not for somebody reading this repository's commit log.
 
 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### Added
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` now validates a tool call's input against the tool's declared `inputSchema`
+  before the tool runs. Input the schema rejects never reaches the executor: the registry returns a
+  tool result describing what was wrong — the failing property path and the constraint that failed,
+  never the offending value — so the model can correct the call on its next round instead of the
+  whole conversation failing with a transport error. Definitions are schema-compiled at
+  registration, so a schema that is not valid JSON Schema fails at startup rather than
+  mid-conversation. Input that passes the schema reaches the executor unchanged: undeclared extra
+  properties are forwarded, types are not coerced and defaults are not injected. An executor that
+  hand-validated its input can stop doing so; a tool that relied on receiving malformed input to
+  produce its own error message now sees only schema-valid input.
+
