@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+# Tool Registry
+
+| Field  | Value   |
+| ------ | ------- |
+| Issue  | n/a     |
+| Status | Shipped |
+
+`ToolRegistry` in `src/orchestration/tools/registry.ts` is the extension point tools are written against: an executor is registered under a name, and consumers resolve, inspect and invoke it through the registry's read surface. Input validation on `execute` is specified separately in `specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md`; the statements here cover the rest of that surface — registration lookup, name checks, and the prompt-facing metadata the engine collects from registered tools.
+
+## Registration lookup
+
+- `ToolRegistry.get` returns the registered tool's resolved definition together with its executor, and returns `undefined` for a name that was never registered ([validated by: exposes a registered tool through get and reports nothing for an unknown name](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L168)).
+- `ToolRegistry.has` reports whether a tool name is currently registered ([validated by: reports whether a name is registered through has](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L213)).
+
+## Prompt-facing metadata
+
+- `getPromptInstructions` and `getExamplePrompts` collect `promptInstructions` and `examplePrompts` from the tools that declare them, one `name: instruction` line per declaring tool, and ignore tools that declare neither ([validated by: collects prompt instructions and example prompts only from tools that declare them](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L189)).
